    "id": "re-foundations-2b-the-hottest-chilies",
    "title": "RE Foundations / 2B / The Hottest Chilies",
    "text_type": "informational",
    "audience": {
      "grade_band": "upper_elementary"
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "You may have experienced the feeling."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "Your mouth feels like it’s on fire."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Your eyes start to water."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "You just ate one of nature’s hottest foods—the chili pepper!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Chili peppers, also called chilies, are found in dishes around the world."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "They are in dishes like Indian curries, Thai tom yum soup, and Mexican enchiladas."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "Chilies come from the capsicum plant."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "They are “hot” because they contain something called capsaicin."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Capsaicin is very good for your health."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "It helps you breathe better, and it may even help keep you fit."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Capsaicin makes you feel less hungry."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "It also makes your body burn more calories."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "We can measure the heat of chilies in units called Scoville heat units (SHU)."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "The world’s hottest chili is the Carolina Reaper."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "It sometimes measures up to 2 million SHU!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "Eating a hot chili can be painful, but some people love to eat them."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "Anandita Dutta Tamuly, a woman from Assam, India, became famous for eating chilies."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "She ate 51 hot peppers in just two minutes!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "The peppers were Naga Jolokia (“ghost peppers”)."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "They grow in Assam and are the third-hottest chilies in the world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "order": 6,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "“I found eating chilies was a great way to stay healthy,” says Tamuly."
          },
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "She began eating chilies when she was a child."
          },
          {
            "id": "s25",
            "text": "She eats chilies when she is sick, too."
          },
          {
            "id": "s26",
            "text": "“Every time I have a cold or flu, I just eat some chilies and I feel better."
          },
          {
            "id": "s27",
            "text": "To be honest, I barely notice them now.”"
          },
          {
            "id": "s34",
            "text": "Chili peppers, also called chilies, are found in dishes around the world."
          },
          {
            "id": "s39",
            "text": "Every time I have a cold or flu, I just eat some chilies and I feel better."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
